# Team 4B Docker build context exclusions (Task 11.1).
#
# Keep the build context small and avoid ever sending secrets, VCS
# metadata, or generated artifacts into the image build. The Dockerfile
# itself only explicitly COPYs app/, requirements.txt, docs/, and
# README.md, so most of this is defense-in-depth rather than strictly
# load-bearing -- but a smaller build context also makes `docker build`
# faster and easier to audit.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Python virtual environments / local interpreter state
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.hypothesis

# Tests -- not part of the runtime image
tests

# Secrets / local environment overrides -- NEVER baked into the image.
# Only *.example files (placeholders only) are ever meant to ship.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.docker.example

# Generated runtime artifacts (Task 9.1's JSONLEvaluationStore output;
# the container creates its own copy of this path fresh, per the
# Dockerfile's own `mkdir -p /app/data`)
data

# IDE / OS metadata
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Docs about this exact packaging step's own review process, not needed
# inside the image itself
*.md.bak
